# ==============================================================================
# CELL CAPTURE, PART 2: the motion gate
# ==============================================================================
# Every motion the capture tool makes -- its own, and the pipeline's when a
# scenario flies the pipeline -- goes through here. APPROVED CELL LIMITS, and
# where each one is enforced:
#
#   * previewed in RViz and confirmed at the prompt before it runs: the ARM
#     going through the motion on /display_planned_path, which the
#     MotionPlanning display in the shipped RViz configs animates, plus the path
#     as a line and the waypoints on /capture/preview_markers and
#     /capture/preview.
#     NO SHIPPED RVIZ CONFIG SUBSCRIBES TO THOSE TWO -- no .rviz in
#     tari_ur_description or tari_ur_soft_launch mentions either topic, so the
#     line and the waypoints are not on screen and only the arm animation is.
#     Adding a MarkerArray display on /capture/preview_markers to
#     view_robot.rviz and view_simbot.rviz is the missing half; until then
#     preview_audience() says so before every confirmation.
#   * at most CAPTURE_SPEED_AWAY away from the part and CAPTURE_SPEED_NEAR near
#     it, enforced three ways (see _Monitor):
#       - BEFORE: the MoveIt scaling is bounded from the joint velocity limits
#         MoveIt itself applies (read from mtc_hub_node), through IK along a
#         Cartesian path or FK along a joint move, so no checked point of the
#         tooling can exceed 0.8-0.85 x the limit; the cell's velocity
#         calibration can only make it slower;
#       - DURING: the tool's speed is measured from TF, in TF's own stamps; above
#         CAPTURE_OVERSPEED_FACTOR x the limit the arm is STOPPED (UR program
#         paused on hardware, the trajectory replaced by a hold in simulation)
#         and the scenario ends;
#       - AFTER: a measured peak above the limit (+CAPTURE_SPEED_TOLERANCE) is
#         reported as OVER THE LIMIT, never "ok", and every later move of that
#         kind is slowed by the measured ratio;
#   * nothing outside the work volume: every straight-line leg is sampled at
#     5 mm and every joint move through FK at 2 degrees, and one sample outside
#     the box refuses the move;
#   * the warning light on (the scenario holds it; see cell_capture_take.dpi).
#
# The pipeline's motions are gated by swapping `ros` for a proxy for the length
# of a scenario (gated_pipeline()); pipeline code looks `ros` up as a global at
# call time, so reconstruct_specimen() and run_automated_scan() run unchanged,
# with every CartesianMove / JointMove / MoveJoints / ApproachInConfiguration /
# FreeMove confirmed.
#
# ONE of those rules is not only for capture sessions. The cable envelope --
# how far wrist 3 may turn before the loom binds -- has to hold on EVERY motion
# this cell makes, scenario or not. install_cable_guard() wraps `ros` for the
# WHOLE session using the same proxy design, with no prompts and only that one
# question; see THE CABLE GUARD at the bottom of this file, and
# cable_envelope.dpi for the model.

# Each .dpi is its own function body: another part's imports are not visible.
